;
; Raw oversampling capture of one WS281x-style pixel-data input line.
;
; Rather than trying to decode WS281x 0/1 bits and FPP v2 inter-segment gaps
; directly in PIO (which would require baking in exact bit-cell timing we
; haven't verified against real hardware yet), this program just samples the
; pin once per clock tick and streams the raw levels out. Bit decoding, gap
; detection, and end-of-frame detection all happen in software (see
; PixelGapReceiver), which can adapt to whatever timing shows up on the wire
; and is far easier to tune/debug without reflashing PIO code.
;
; Sample rate is set by the state machine clock divider from the C side
; (GapCapture::begin). ~4Msps gives ~5 samples per bit at WS2812 (800kHz)
; timing and ~10 samples per bit at WS2811 (400kHz) timing -- plenty of
; resolution to classify short vs. long pulses either way.

.program gap_capture

.wrap_target
    in pins, 1
.wrap
